<title>INDIA: Delhi shares weak on foreign selling.</title>
<headline>Delhi shares weak on foreign selling.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares on the Delhi bourse lost further ground at mid-session, pressed by heavy selling by foreign institutional investors (FIIs) and profit-takers, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1.00 p.m.(0730 GMT), the Delhi sensitive index was 6.01 points down at 641.94.</p>
<p>Naresh Kumar of brokers Multiple investments said speculators sold heavily at higher levels.</p>
<p>ACC lost 10 rupees at 990.</p>
<p>TELCO fell 5.75 rupees to 308.25.</p>
<p>Hindustan Lever dropped 10 rupees to 775.</p>
<p>ITC fell 4.05 rupees to 275.</p>
<p>Reliance Industries fell 1.15 rupees to 186.25.</p>
<p>Larsen and Toubro dropped 0.80 rupee to 205.80.</p>
<p>State Bank of India dropped 1.65 rupees to 207.25.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91 11- 301 2024</p>
